sentences.text:
The petitioner is before this Court seeking the following prayers:
"
(a) Issue Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or directions to the Respondent No.1 and Respondent No.2 to immediately complete the sale 605 acres allotted land at the offered price without any restriction as to user and convey clear and unrestricted title to the 605 acres of land at Hassan allotted to the petitioner and complete registration formalities and physical handing over of the land to the petitioner at the agreed cost;
(b) Issue Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or directions to the Respondent No. 1 to refund a sum of Rs.6,05,00,000 (Six Crores and Five lakhs only) being the amount deposited by the Petitioner, with interest @ 18% from the date of the deposit to the Petitioner;
(c) Issue Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or directions to allow Petitioner to inspect the 605 acres of land and its title located at Hassan and then complete its purchase in a period as this Hon'ble Court deems fit after allowing prayer (a);
Hassan Thermal Power Private Limited vs Karnataka Industrial Areas ... on 7 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/86110561/
2 (d) Issue Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or directions to the Respondent No.1 to pay 18% interest on Rs.6,05,00,000 (Six Crores and Five lakhs only) from the respective date of deposit of the said amount by the Petitioner to the Respondent No.1;
(e) Issue Writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or directions to the Respondent No.1 to compensate the Petitioner to the tune of Rs.150,00,000 (One hundred fifty crores) for the false misrepresentation made by Respondent No.1 as to the acquisition of the land and Rs.50,00,000 (Fifty lakhs) for the delay of more than a decade in refunding the advance payments made by the Petitioner against the allotment of land at Hassan;
(f) Direct the Respondent No.1 to pay Rs.15,00,000 (Fifteen Lakhs) as litigation costs; AND (g) Pass any such order/orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and necessary in the circumstances of the present Petition."
2. This Court, on hearing the parties, had passed slew of interim orders.

